WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.700
TenkaCloud Lite lets one organizer run an event in their AWS account. Here is the whole flow.

2
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.500
The CloudFormation stack invokes CodeBuild to run CDK deploy.

3
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.800
Upload the template so CloudFormation creates the automatic deployment setup.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.200
Press Start build, then confirm the automatic Lite deployment and its URLs.

5
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.900
Open the Admin Console from the invite email.

6
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:35.100
Keep operations and competitor AWS separate, then connect them with an external I D.

7
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:45.233
Register the competitor AWS account, create its bootstrap stack, then verify the trust.

8
00:00:45.433 --> 00:00:49.933
An event connects the team, AWS account, and problem before deployment.

9
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:57.433
Create an event, then assign the verified account and the problem to play.

10
00:00:57.633 --> 00:01:02.133
Select deploy, then wait until the problem stack is ready.

11
00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:11.233
Sign in to Participant Portal with the team key.

12
00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:16.133
Read the problem and submit through its answer field. The answer is not shown.

13
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:19.933
Confirm the Scoreboard update to finish.
